# Reproduction vs. replication

This study is a **replication**, not a bit-exact reproduction. In the NASEM (2019)
terminology, *reproduction* re-runs the same code on the same data; *replication*
re-derives a paper's findings with **independent methods and independently sourced
data** — which is what this is (independent tvbo → backend implementation on open data).
It reproduces the paper's *qualitative claims and structural invariants*; quantities
depending on unpublished realizations or rendering choices differ, as expected.

